@d1kan One thing stands out: 333000 sectors is the 74-minute value, and your disc is 80 minutes. On the same ATIP (97m26s66f), nyannurs measured 359,846 usable sectors at the top of this thread. With the wrong count the program expects the wrong spiral. Concentric circles would survive that, because they depend mainly on radius, while radial lines fall apart, which matches what you're seeing.

Please try "Read from disc" on the calibration page with a blank disc in the drive, and generate the target with the count it reports. If DiscImageStudio reports 333000 for this disc, that would be worth showing here.

We have CD-Rs with the same ATIP, and read timing puts their geometry noticeably away from the built-in Verbatim AZO preset. I don't want to send you numbers we haven't checked on a burned disc, so I'll post them here once we have.

