I purchased DVD-R discs (manufactured by RITEK) under the BUFFALO brand in Amazon JP.
As luck would have it? I received an almost identical disc. (Hajime0512 got the DR5F6O-50013, while I received the DR5F6O-50012.)

<img width="686" height="297" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f9bb6f07-16a9-428e-9c0b-b87219ccf5c7" />

The sector count reported by the optical drive did not match, so I had to recalculate it.
(2,297,888 vs. 2,298,496 free sectors; ref: https://forum.imgburn.com/topic/21527-2297888-vs-2298496-free-sectors/)

Following this calculation, the test pattern written to the disc appeared distorted (disc on the left); however, after performing further calibration, I was able to achieve more stable results (disc on the right).

<img width="1702" height="1179" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/31805a21-215a-4015-9baf-54a577f84f3b" />

```csharp
using DiscImageStudio.Core;
using System.Globalization;
CultureInfo.CurrentCulture = CultureInfo.InvariantCulture;

const double bitNm = 133.3; const int bitsPerSector = 38688;
double r0 = 24.015314703488574, r1 = 58.124649934344262;
double c1 = 2.4729772497054432E-05, c2 = -4.8023791953470689E-05, c3 = 2.666661601004263E-05;
long n = 2298496, n2 = 2297888;
double L(long s) => s * (double)bitsPerSector * bitNm * 1e-6;

var g = DvdTrackGeometry.Create(r0, r1, L(n), c1, c2, c3);
double r1b = g.RadiusAtArcLength(L(n2));
double k = (r1b - r0) / (r1 - r0);
double d1 = c1 * k, d2 = c2 * k * k, d3 = c3 * k * k * k;
var h = DvdTrackGeometry.Create(r0, r1b, L(n2), d1, d2, d3);

Console.WriteLine($"r1'   = {r1b:R}");
Console.WriteLine($"c1'   = {d1:R}");
Console.WriteLine($"c2'   = {d2:R}");
Console.WriteLine($"c3'   = {d3:R}");
Console.WriteLine($"growth orig={g.RadialGrowthPerRadianMm:R} new={h.RadialGrowthPerRadianMm:R}");

// Compare sector -> (r, angle) of the new geometry with the original one.
double maxDr = 0, maxDturn = 0;
for (long s = 0; s <= n2; s += 997)
{
    double a = L(s);
    var (ra, ta) = g.AtArcLengthFast(a);
    var (rb, tb) = h.AtArcLengthFast(a);
    maxDr = Math.Max(maxDr, Math.Abs(ra - rb));
    maxDturn = Math.Max(maxDturn, Math.Abs(ta - tb) / (2 * Math.PI));
}
Console.WriteLine($"max |dr| = {maxDr:E3} mm, max |dθ| = {maxDturn:E3} turns");

// Naive approach: only change the sector count, keep r0/r1/coefficients.
var naive = DvdTrackGeometry.Create(r0, r1, L(n2), c1, c2, c3);
var (_, tn) = naive.AtArcLengthFast(L(n2));
var (_, to) = g.AtArcLengthFast(L(n2));
Console.WriteLine($"naive (sector count only) angle error at end = {(tn - to) / (2 * Math.PI):F2} turns");
```

